  "text": "proprium.sanctissimae-trinitatis-evangelium",
  "about": "The Gospel of the feast of the Most Holy Trinity, Matthew 28:18–20. The risen Christ sends the disciples to teach and baptize in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Ghost.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "At that time Jesus said to His disciples: All power is given to Me in heaven and on earth." },
    "s02": { "translation": "Going therefore, teach ye all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Ghost; teaching them to observe all things whatsoever I have commanded you." },
    "s03": { "translation": "And behold, I am with you all days, even to the consummation of the world." }
  },
